sentences.l:
and sacred Onchestus, Poseidon’s splendid grove,
and who held Arne rich in grapes, and who Mideia
and most holy Nisa and Anthedon lying at the edge;

and who inhabited around Anemoreia and Hyampolis,
and who beside the river Cephisus, heavenly, dwelt,
and who held Lilaea at the springs of Cephisus;

And of the Locrians was leader, of Oileus, swift Ajax,
the smaller, not at all so big as Telamonian Ajax,
but much smaller;

who inhabited Cynus and Opoeis and Calliarus
and Bessa and Scarphe and lovely Augeiae
and Tarphe and Thronium, about the streams of the Boagrius;

And with him the Abantes followed, swift, long-haired behind,
spearmen, eager with outstretched ash-spears
to break the breastplates of enemies about their chests;

and set him down in Athens, in her own rich temple;
and there with bulls and with rams they appease him,
the young men of the Athenians, as the years come round;
